{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["If it were written \"in the camp,\" it would be permissible to slaughter it outside the camp, and this commandment depends also on the Temple, except in any place that is near Jerusalem. And what is \"near\" we know from received tradition, for if the place were far, one slaughters and eats meat, for so it is written. And many say that meat is forbidden in exile, and they expound \"meat and wine did not come into my mouth\" (Daniel 10:3) — as referring to meat of fish — but they did not speak correctly, and I do not wish to elaborate to refute them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:34.224033008Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}